{"kind":"request","text":"Bring apps/room/wrangler.demo.jsonc up to date with dap-demo's Register 26 settings\n\ndap-demo has served Register 26 with Register 17 still installed since 00:08 on 6 November. The checked-in apps/room/wrangler.demo.jsonc still selects Register 17 only, so a deploy from it would make dap-demo single-root again and strand the new rooms' Git hosting. Until this lands, the planner deploys dap-demo only from the rendered offer configuration (SHA-256 14fb81a1…).\n\nThe live record under review (request ba5e2a8d, head e4f26d83) lists the four settings that differ: REGISTER_SCOPE, INSTALLED_REGISTER_SCOPES, ARTIFACTS_CONFIG's registerScope and DEMO_START_CONFIG. Their values are in its \"Source and settings\" table. Nothing else differs except main, which stays worker.ts.\n\nIn one head:\n1. Set those four values in apps/room/wrangler.demo.jsonc and update packages/cli/test/demo-config.test.ts to pin them.\n2. The packet's render.mjs pins the old file's digest (packet.json baseConfigSha256 87bb65bb…), so it will refuse the new file. The packet becomes historical. Say in the packet's deploy.md that the rollback there applies only to the 6 November switch, and what rollback means from the synced file: a rollback must never drop either root.\n3. Fix token-clone.mjs's two remote assertions to the Artifacts host the CLI actually clones from (the planner ran a corrected copy, sha256 dba7ef31, recorded as a deviation).\n4. Show with a Wrangler dry run, from a scratch tool directory, that the synced file and the offer configuration produce the same bindings and vars.\n\nRun the focused tests for what you change and the gate once before review. No deploy: the planner deploys dap-demo from the landed file and checks health, the offer and an old room's Site. Never run rm -rf or rm -f.","body":{"conditions":"One reviewed head on main makes the checked-in dap-demo configuration equal to the live offer settings, pins them in the demo config test, marks the packet historical with the rollback rule, and fixes the observer's host assertion; checker-approved and landed.","target_head":"e50d9eebb27f47d0f33549486751ab8bdce8de80","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}